# Deliberately NOT `complete:check`. That runs the unit, integration and contract suites, which
# take minutes — long enough that people reach for `--no-verify`, and a hook that gets bypassed
# protects nothing. CI already runs every one of those as its own parallel job, so the only thing
# a commit hook adds is catching what would be embarrassing in a diff: a type error, a lint error,
# unformatted code. Those are seconds, and they are the ones worth blocking on.
#
# Before pushing (or opening a PR), run the real gate by hand: `npm run complete:check`.
npm run complete:fast
